# Not required by api/[...path].js's dependency graph or the build —
# safe to exclude from the deployment entirely rather than leaving them
# publicly downloadable at their literal paths.
supabase/

# Note: server.js, server-app.js, db.js, auth-mw.js, mailer.js, sms.js,
# matching.js, lib/, routes/, package.json, and package-lock.json are
# NOT listed here — they're genuine dependencies of api/[...path].js
# (or, for the two package files, required for Vercel to install those
# dependencies) and excluding them would break the deployed function.
# Whether those files end up separately reachable as static assets at
# their literal paths is a real open question this .vercelignore does
# not fully resolve — verify against a Vercel Preview deploy before
# treating server-side source exposure as closed. See supabase/SETUP.md.
